// The boss journal: Caelum Vey, the Starborn, the calm swordsman at the heart of the crater, in each hero's own words (docs/plans/journal-voices.md)
// Caelum has one spoken line as the fight begins, but the journals leave it out like every other boss line; the heroes speak for him. Move keys are cast names (the journal fires on the cast bar's name).
// The idea every page carries: he appears before he cuts, so read the silver afterimages (their order and their facing) and a dance nobody has seen can still be read. The meteor's shadow on the floor is the clock.
// Nightfall is the cast that follows Grace Withdrawn, and the pages for the two go together. Ascendant is the change to the cloud, and Horizon Cut belongs to that second form.
// Mirrored Wake, Second Coil and Dark Ember are the Hard-only pages. Chorus of the Fallen is in every difficulty's last dance (and one copy joins each act on Hard).
(window.JOURNAL_DATA = window.JOURNAL_DATA || {}).caelum = {
  // the first time this hero meets him (after the first pull)
  meet: {
    bastion: "A swordsman in black glass who walks and never runs, with a ring of broken stars turning at his back. Before each cut a silver copy of him stands where he will be, and the copies show the order and the way he faces. Read them. The shadow on the floor grows. Held.",
    gloomsworn: "A tall man in black glass and a silver mask, a ring of broken stars at his back. He shows himself before he cuts: a silver copy stands where he will be, facing the way he will go next. The meteor's shadow grows each time. I know a clock when I see one.",
    thresher: "Such a quiet, tall gentleman in black glass, dear, with a halo of broken stars. He turns up before he cuts: a silver copy of him stands where he will be, facing the way he will go. Read the copies and you can read the dance. The shadow on the floor grows. Off we go.",
    bloodreaver: "The glass one just stands there, calm as a stone, and every cut comes after a silver copy of him shows where he'll be! Read the copies, their order and which way they face, and the dance is plain. The meteor's shadow keeps growing. A fine scar, when I read it right.",
    runeguard: "The omen: before every cut, a silver copy of him stands where he will be, facing the way the next will lie. The answer: read the copies, in order, and a dance never seen before is plain. The meteor's shadow on the floor is the clock. As foreseen.",
    gorgemaw: "My host is a calm, glassy fellow who plates every course in advance: a silver copy of him stands where the knife will fall, facing the next. Read the copies and you know the menu. The meteor's shadow widens on the floor like a stain. Promising, and far too tidy.",
    oathbroker: "The counterparty gives notice before he acts: a silver copy of him stands where he will stand, its facing naming the next. The fine print is that the copies are the whole contract. Read them. The meteor's shadow on the floor grows with each clause. So noted.",
    ironpalm: "Caelum does not strike without speaking first. A silver copy of him stands where he will be, and its face shows the next. I read the copies like a sentence. The shadow under the sky grows with every word. Breathe.",
    ranger: "Tall, still, black glass, silver mask. It shows itself before it cuts: a silver copy at each spot, facing the next. Read the order, read the facing, find the open ground. Meteor's shadow on the floor grows every stage. Clean line.",
    shadowblade: "The mark never hides, which is rude. A silver copy of him stands where he will be before every cut, and it faces where he will go next. Read the copies and you know the dance, and where its blind sides are. The sky's shadow grows. It never saw me. I saw it first.",
    pyromancer: "He's beautiful, and so calm it's insulting! Before every cut a silver copy of him stands where he'll be, facing the next, so I read the copies like an order of lighting. The meteor's shadow on the floor keeps growing. Mostly unsinged, so far.",
    thermist: "Cold read: he shows himself before he cuts, a silver copy at each spot, facing the next. Read the order and the dance is plain. Hot read: the meteor's shadow on the floor keeps growing, and I felt it in my teeth. Back to the middle.",
    driftblade: "He walks, never runs, and before every cut a silver copy of him stands where he'll be, facing the next, so I read the copies and picked my way through the dance, round the ends and through the gaps, while the meteor's shadow crept wider on the floor.",
    alembist: "Specimen: tall, black glass, still. Observed: a silver copy of him stands where he will be before each cut, facing the next. Note: read the order and the facing, and the dance is plain. Label: the shadow on the floor, growing. A clock, and I do like clocks.",
    threadweaver: "He goes about it like a tailor chalking cloth: a silver copy of him stands where each cut will fall, and its face points to the next. Read the chalk and nobody is cut. The shadow of the sky on the floor grows wider every stage. Mind the slack.",
    marionettist: "Our leading man never rushes. Before each cut a silver copy of him takes his mark, facing the next: the blocking, chalked in advance. Read the marks and the dance is plain. The meteor's shadow spreads across the stage. (Every cut rehearsed in plain sight.)",
    cleric: "Poor young man, all glass and silver, and so calm. Before he cuts, a silver copy of him stands where he will be, facing the way he will go next. We read them and nobody was cut. The shadow of the sky on the floor grows. Dawn keep us.",
    grovekeeper: "A calm one, like the stillness before a storm. He shows himself before he cuts: a silver copy at each spot, facing the next. Read the sky before the weather. The meteor's shadow on the floor grows like frost across a pond. Plant first.",
    chronomancer: "He appears before he cuts, which is the sort of order I admire. A silver copy of him stands where he will be, facing the next, so I read the dance a beat ahead and will have been there. The shadow of the sky grows. A clock, and not mine.",
    tidecaller: "A still shore of a man, and the tide comes in on him slowly: the meteor's shadow on the floor grows wider each time the water turns. He shows himself before he cuts, a silver copy at each spot, facing the next. Read the swell. Mind the tide.",
    lanternkeeper: "A tall man in black glass who lets us see every step first: a silver copy of him stands where he will be, facing the next. I read them, and went where the floor was clear. The meteor's shadow on the floor kept widening. Keep your light.",
    kenseier: "Caelum walks, and before each cut a silver copy of him stands where the stroke will end, facing the next. That is a count I can read. The meteor's shadow on the floor grows as the beats go by. He is honest about his cuts. Catch the beat.",
    houndmaster: "Tall lad in black glass, calm as a stone. Shows himself before he cuts: a silver copy at the spot, facing the next. Read them and the dogs and I know where to be. The shadow of the big fire up top grows on the floor. Heel.",
  },
  // the first time this hero beats him
  win: {
    bastion: "The Starborn is down. The shadow on the floor is gone, and the sky has let go of the meteor, which broke into falling stars over the whole realm. We held the ground to the end. Will hold.",
    gloomsworn: "He is down, and the meteor broke apart in the sky and fell as stars over every road we have walked. The shadow is gone from the floor. I watched them fall. The dead would have liked the view.",
    thresher: "He's down, dear, and the sky has let go: the meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm, and the shadow is gone from the floor. A lovely appointment, and kept. His name is off the list. In time, for all of us!",
    bloodreaver: "He's down! The meteor broke in the sky and rained down as stars over the whole realm, and the shadow on the floor went out. I bled a good deal for that sky, my friend, and would again. A fine scar.",
    runeguard: "The Starborn is fallen, and it is entered in the margin: the shadow lifted from the floor, and the meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm. Every omen read; every dance foreseen in the end. As foreseen.",
    gorgemaw: "My host is down, and the sky has changed its menu: the meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm. The shadow is gone from the floor. A grand last course, though I would have eaten the star. Nearly full.",
    oathbroker: "The Starborn is concluded: felled, the shadow lifted from the floor, and the meteor broken into falling stars over the whole realm. The sky's account is discharged. Entered in the ledger. Countersigned.",
    ironpalm: "Caelum fell, and the sky fell silent after him. The meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm, and the shadow left the floor. He spoke before every cut, and we answered each word. I breathed.",
    ranger: "Down. Shadow gone from the floor. Meteor broke apart overhead and came down as stars across the whole realm. Watched them from the rim. Clean line.",
    shadowblade: "The mark is down, the shadow gone from the floor, and the meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm. He showed himself before every cut and still never saw me. It never saw me.",
    pyromancer: "He's down, and the meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm! The best fireworks I have ever stood under, and I had a hand in them. Shadow gone, sleeves gone. Mostly unsinged.",
    thermist: "Down. Cold: the shadow gone from the floor. Hot: the meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm, and I wept a little. I am exactly the temperature of the room again. Back to the middle.",
    driftblade: "He's down and the meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm and I ran under the first of them, through the clear floor where the shadow had been, round and round and never landing, and laughed till I had to sit.",
    alembist: "Specimen: felled; the shadow gone from the floor. The meteor broke apart in the sky and fell as stars over the whole realm. Flasks intact. One bright grain of it, in a jar. Label: the Starborn, spent. Never so pleased.",
    threadweaver: "He's down, the shadow gone from the floor, and the meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm, like a hem coming undone in the best way. Come and sit by me, the whole lot of you. Kettle's on.",
    marionettist: "Final curtain for our leading man. The shadow left the boards and the meteor broke into falling stars over the whole house, the realm entire. (The Doll bowed first. The company agreed.)",
    cleric: "He is at rest, poor young man, and the sky has let go of the meteor. It broke into falling stars over the whole realm, and the shadow left the floor. I said a prayer for him, and one for all of us. Thank the light.",
    grovekeeper: "He's down, dear, and the sky let go of its stone. The meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm, and the shadow left the floor like frost under the sun. Sit. Tea. Plant first.",
    chronomancer: "He fell, and nothing needed undoing. The shadow lifted and the meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm. I will have watched them fall. I did. It was worth the long way round.",
    tidecaller: "He is down and the shadow has drawn off the floor like a tide gone out. The meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm. I sang under them, low. The sea gives back, and so, at last, did the sky.",
    lanternkeeper: "He is down. The shadow lifted off the floor, and the meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm. I lit one small lamp where the shadow had been and left it burning. Walk where it's warm.",
    kenseier: "Caelum is down, the shadow gone from the floor, and the meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm. The last stroke was ours, and he bowed his head to it. I bowed to him. Ash settles.",
    houndmaster: "Tall lad's down, shadow gone off the floor, meteor broke into falling stars over the whole realm. Dogs fine. Stood and watched them come down. Good dogs. We had him by supper.",
  },
  moves: {
    'Glint': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "One silver copy of him stood far across the floor, and a line was drawn to it from his feet. He was gone from his place and there in a blink. It was aimed at one of the others, who stepped sideways off the line. The cut found empty floor. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "A single silver copy stood across the room and a line ran to it. He was there before the line had finished drawing. Whoever it was aimed at stepped off its edge. I did not move; it was not for me. I have stood in worse lines.",
      thresher: "One silver copy, dear, far across the floor, and a line drawn to it from his feet. He is there before you can say hello. Whoever the line points at steps off it, sideways, and it cuts the floor instead. Do mind the step.",
      bloodreaver: "A silver copy of him way off, and a line drawn to it! One of the others had the line aimed at them and stepped off it, sideways. He cut empty floor and looked almost embarrassed. Don't stand in his road, my friend. Shameful, for him.",
      runeguard: "The omen: a single silver copy at the end of a drawn line, facing away from him. The answer: the cut runs down the line and ends where the copy stands, so whoever it points at steps off the line, sideways. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "A single silver copy at the end of a drawn line, like a garnish set down before the dish. The cut ran down the line to it. The guest it pointed at simply stepped aside. A thin, quick course. Still hungry.",
      oathbroker: "Notice was served first: a single silver copy at the far end of a drawn line. The clause is that the cut runs the whole length and he ends at the far end. The party it names steps outside the line. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "A line and one silver copy at its end. A short word, said plainly: he would be there. Whoever it pointed at stepped off the line, and the cut spoke to the floor. Then we answered him. Breathe.",
      ranger: "One silver copy at the far end of a drawn line. Cut runs the length of it. Aimed at one of us, who stepped to the flank. Never take the line; take the side. He ends at the far end. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "A single silver copy at the end of a line, and he followed it there in a blink, which is showing off. It was aimed at someone else, who stepped off the line, and I came in at his side after. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "One silver copy way across the floor and a line drawn to it, glowing the colour of trouble! He crossed it in a blink. Whoever it was pointing at stepped off, and I kept clear of the road and kept casting. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Cold read: one silver copy at the far end of a line. The cut runs the line and ends at the copy. Step off its edge. Hot read: I stood in a line once, and felt it all the way through. Off the line. Back to the middle.",
      driftblade: "A single silver copy at the end of a line and then he was gone from his place and in it, and whoever the line pointed at had already gone sideways off it, and I went round behind him through the space he'd left, never landing.",
      alembist: "Ailment: one line, one silver copy at its end, a cut the whole length. Remedy: whoever it points at steps off its edge. Note: he is at the far end afterward. Label: sideways, never back.",
      threadweaver: "One silver copy at the far end of a line, like a pin set before the cut. He ran the seam in a blink, and whoever the line pointed at stepped off the edge of it. A neat stitch, if you're not in it. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "One silver copy at the end of a line: his mark, taken first. He crossed in a blink. The player it was aimed at stepped off the line. (Exit, sideways. Nobody is cut who leaves in time.)",
      cleric: "A single silver copy at the far end of a line, and he was there in a heartbeat. It was aimed at one of my dears, who stepped sideways off the line, and the cut found only floor. Dawn keep us.",
      grovekeeper: "One silver copy at the end of a line, like a seed dropped far off. He was there in a blink. Whoever the line pointed to stepped sideways off it, and it cut bare floor. As easy as a dodged frost. Plant first.",
      chronomancer: "The copy stands first, the line is drawn, and a beat after he is there. Whoever it points at steps off the line in the beat between. I will have stepped already; I did, sideways. Well, mostly.",
      tidecaller: "One silver copy far across the floor and a line drawn to it, like a rip running out. He crossed it in a blink. Whoever it pointed at stepped out of the current, sideways, and the cut broke on the shore. Mind the tide.",
      lanternkeeper: "A single silver copy at the end of a drawn line, and he was there in a blink. I watched who it was aimed at and set a light just off the line, so they stepped toward it. It cut bare floor. A light for each of us.",
      kenseier: "One line, one silver copy at its end. The stroke runs the line with no beat to turn: a blade cannot meet a thing that has gone and arrived. Whoever it points at steps off the edge. A courtesy to show it first.",
      houndmaster: "One silver copy way off, line drawn to it. He crossed it in a blink. Pointed at one of us, who stepped off sideways. Kept the dogs out of the road. Sit. Cut the floor, that's all. Heel.",
    } },
    'Eightfold Wake': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Silver copies ringed the whole room, each facing the next he would cut to. The lines were all drawn before the first fell. I read the order, found ground no line crossed, and held it. Cut ground is safe. A ring of light swept us all at the last cut; I braced. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "Silver copies all round the room, each facing the next, and every line painted before he moved. I followed the order and found the floor nothing crossed. Cut ground was safe to stand. At the last cut a ring of light ran over us all, a small hurt; the healer had us up first.",
      thresher: "A ring of silver copies, dear, each facing the next, every line painted before the first cut. Read the order, find the floor no line crosses; a line already cut is safe. At the last cut a ring of light runs over us all, a small hurt, so be mended before. Off we go.",
      bloodreaver: "The room filled with silver copies, each facing the next, and every cut drawn before it came! I followed the order, stayed off the lines, and stood on ground already cut, since the same stroke never lands twice. The last cut sent a ring of light over all of us. Mend up before, healer.",
      runeguard: "The omen: a ring of silver copies, each facing the next, every cut drawn ahead. The answer: follow the order, stand where no line crosses, and a line already cut is safe ground. When the last cut lands a ring of light crosses the room, a small hurt; be mended before. Now foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "A banquet of silver copies round the room, each facing the next, every course drawn before it was served. Follow the order, sit where no line crosses, and a line already cut is a plate already cleared. A ring of light was the garnish after the last cut, a small hurt. Overdressed, but honest.",
      oathbroker: "The schedule was served in advance: a ring of silver copies, each facing the next, every line drawn. follow the order, stand where no line crosses, and ground already cut is discharged. The fine print: a ring of light crosses the room at the last cut, a small sum; be mended beforehand. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "A sentence of silver copies round the room, each facing the next word, every line drawn before it was spoken. I followed the order and stood where no line crossed. A line already spoken is silent ground. At the last word a ring of light crossed the room, a small hurt. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Silver copies ringed the room, each facing the next. Lines drawn before the first cut. Followed the order, found floor nothing crossed, then went to ground that had already been cut. Cut ground is safe. Last cut sends a ring of light across the whole room, a small hurt; be mended before. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "A ring of silver copies, each facing the next, every line drawn before he moved, which was rude. I read the order, kept to floor no line crossed, and slipped onto cut ground behind him. At the last cut a ring of light crossed the room, a small sting. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "The room filled with silver copies, each facing the next, every line glowing in advance! I followed the order, found floor no line crossed, and resented every step, but cut ground is safe to stand on. The last cut sent a ring of light across the room, a small hurt. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Cold read: silver copies, each facing the next, every line drawn first. Follow the order, find floor no line crosses. Hot read: a line already cut is safe, so I ran onto it, breathless. The last cut sent a ring of light over the room; a small hurt; mend before. Back to the middle.",
      driftblade: "Silver copies all round the room, each facing the next, every line drawn before the first cut, so I followed the order with my eyes and went through the gaps and over ground already cut, and never landed, though the ring of light after the last cut caught us all, a little.",
      alembist: "Ailment: a ring of silver copies, each facing the next; every line drawn before the first cut. Remedy: follow the order, stand where no line crosses, and move onto ground already cut. Note: a ring of light follows the last cut, a small dose for all; brew the mending before. Label: read, then step.",
      threadweaver: "Silver copies pinned round the room, each facing the next, every seam chalked before the first cut. I followed the order and found the cloth no seam crossed, and the seams already cut were safe. The last cut sends a ring of light over the hem, a small tug; mended before. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "A ring of silver copies, each facing the next: the blocking drawn on the boards before the curtain. I followed the order, kept off every line, took my mark on ground already cut. (Exit, the lines. At the last cut a ring of light sweeps the house, a small hurt; mend the company before.)",
      cleric: "A ring of silver copies round the room, each facing the next, every cut drawn first. I followed the order, kept my dears off the lines, and told them cut ground is safe. A ring of light after the last cut hurts us all a little, so I mended them before. Thank the light.",
      grovekeeper: "Silver copies round the room like standing stones, each facing the next, every line drawn first. I followed the order and stood where none crossed. Ground already cut is safe, like a field after the plough. A ring of light sweeps us at the last cut, a small frost; plant the mending before.",
      chronomancer: "Silver copies, each facing the next, every cut drawn first, so the dance is a tune I could hum ahead. I followed the order and stood where no line crossed, then on cut ground. A ring of light comes with the last cut, a small hurt; mend a beat before. I'll have known that.",
      tidecaller: "Silver copies round the room, each facing the next, every line drawn first, like waves lined to break. I followed the order, found the water no line crossed, and stepped on after. A ring of light ran out at the last cut, a small swell; I let the water rise before. Mind the tide.",
      lanternkeeper: "Silver copies ringed the room, each facing the next, every line drawn first. I walked the order with my eyes and lit the ground no line crossed, and ground already cut. A ring of light ran out at the last cut and hurt us a little, so I topped up the wicks before.",
      kenseier: "A ring of silver copies, each facing the next, and a count to every cut. I followed it, stood where no line crossed, and stepped onto cut ground. Nothing to meet. The last cut sends a ring of light across the room, no beat to turn, a small hurt. Mend before. Catch the beat.",
      houndmaster: "Ring of silver copies round the room, each facing the next. Every line drawn first. Followed the order, found floor nothing crossed, dogs tight at my heel. Cut ground's safe after. Last cut sends a ring of light over the lot of us, dogs too, small hurt. Healer got us up before. Heel.",
    } },
    'Anchored Wake': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Two of the silver copies formed where two of us were standing, so we had set part of his dance. The lines ran through those spots. We left them early, and read the rest as before. The last cut sent a ring of light over us all, a small hurt; I braced. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "Two silver copies appeared where two of us stood, as though written into the dance. The lines ran through those places, so we left before the cuts and read the rest as usual. After the last cut a ring of light ran over us all, a small hurt; the healer had us up first.",
      thresher: "Two silver copies formed right where two of us were standing, dear! The lines ran through those spots, so we stepped away early and read the rest of the order as usual. The last cut sends a ring of light over us all, a small hurt, so be mended before. Not yet!",
      bloodreaver: "Two copies of him stood up right where two of my friends were standing! The cuts ran through those spots, so we got off them early and read the rest as usual. I like a dance that learns our names. The last cut's ring of light, a tickle for all. Mend before, healer.",
      runeguard: "The omen: two silver copies form where two of us stand, so the dance is half our own writing. The answer: leave those spots before the cuts run through them, and read the rest as before. The last cut sends a ring of light over all, a small hurt; be mended before. Now foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "My host let two of his silver copies form where two guests sat, so they became part of the dish. The lines ran through those seats. We rose early and read the rest of the courses. A ring of light after the last cut was the garnish, a small hurt. Ill-mannered, but pointed.",
      oathbroker: "A rider to the schedule: two silver copies form where two of the undersigned stand, binding us into the dance. The lines run through those places. We vacated them early, and read the rest as before. The last cut also levies a ring of light on all, a small sum; mended beforehand. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "Two silver copies spoke where two of us stood, and the lines ran through those places. He had asked us to take part. We stepped aside early, and read the rest of the order as before. The last word was a ring of light over all of us, a small hurt. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Two copies formed on the spots two of us were standing. Cuts ran through those spots. Left early, read the rest of the order as before. Last cut sends a ring of light over everyone, small hurt; be mended before. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "Two silver copies formed where two of us were standing, which is cheeky. The lines ran through those spots, so we slipped off early and read the rest of the order as usual. A ring of light crossed the room at the last cut, a small sting for all. It never saw me leave.",
      pyromancer: "Two silver copies formed exactly where two of us were standing, and the lines glowed straight through us! We stepped off those spots early and read the rest of the order as usual. The last cut sent a ring of light across us all, a small singe. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Cold read: two silver copies formed where two of us stood. The lines ran through those spots. Move before the cuts. Hot read: I hate being someone else's corner. Left early, read the rest. A ring of light ran over us at the last cut; a small hurt, mended before. Back to the middle.",
      driftblade: "Two silver copies formed where two of us were standing so the lines ran through those spots and we were gone from them before the first cut, through the gaps, reading the rest as we ran, never landing on a copy, though the ring of light after the last cut caught us, a little.",
      alembist: "Ailment: two silver copies form where two of us stand; the lines pass through those places. Remedy: leave early, then read the rest of the order as before. Note: a ring of light follows the last cut; a small dose for all, so brew the mending before. Label: your own footprint, avoided.",
      threadweaver: "Two silver copies pinned themselves where two of my stitches were standing, so the seam ran through them. We stepped off early and read the rest as before. A sloppy seam, to mark us. The last cut sends a ring of light over the hem, a small tug; mended before. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "Two silver copies took their marks where two of the company stood: a surprise cue. The lines ran through those spots, so we cleared them early and read the rest of the blocking. (Exit, two players, quickly. The last cut sweeps the house with a ring of light, a small hurt; mended before.)",
      cleric: "Two silver copies formed where two of my dears were standing, and the cuts ran through those very places. I called them off early, and we read the rest as before. A ring of light follows the last cut and hurts us all a little, so I mended them before. Dawn keep us.",
      grovekeeper: "Two silver copies sprang where two of my lot were standing, like seeds in the wrong furrow. The lines ran through those spots, so we stepped off early and read the rest as usual. A ring of light sweeps us at the last cut, a small frost; plant the mending before. Plant first.",
      chronomancer: "The dance includes where we stand, which is rude. Two silver copies formed on two of us, the lines through those places. We left a beat early and read the rest as usual. A ring of light comes with the last cut, a small hurt; I mend a beat before. I'll have been gone already.",
      tidecaller: "Two silver copies rose where two of us were standing, like a wave lifting a boat. The lines ran through them. We stepped aside early and read the rest as before. A ring of light ran out at the last cut, a small swell; I let the water rise before. Wait for the water.",
      lanternkeeper: "Two silver copies formed where two of us were standing, with a line through each. I hung a light on a clear spot so they knew where to go, and we read the rest as before. A ring of light crossed the room at the last cut, so I topped up the wicks before.",
      kenseier: "Two silver copies formed where two of us stood, which makes the dance ours. The cuts ran through those places. We stepped aside on the count, and read the rest as before. The last cut sends a ring of light over all, no beat to turn, a small hurt. Mend before. Catch the beat.",
      houndmaster: "Two silver copies sprang up where two of us stood. Lines through those spots. Whistled the dogs clear, stepped off early, read the rest of the order as usual. Last cut sends a ring of light over the lot of us, dogs too, small hurt. Healer had us up before. Sit. Good dogs.",
    } },
    'Cinder Crown': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "A crown of embers closed round me alone. I waited for the glow and took it, shield up in the last instant; the others kept clear of the circle at my feet. Embers then fell on all of us, a little each. It left a ring of fire, so I took it elsewhere. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "The crown of embers was meant for me. I let it land whole and the others stood clear of the circle at my feet. A ring of fire stays where it falls, so I had walked away first. Embers fell on us all after, a little each. I have worn heavier crowns.",
      thresher: "A crown of embers around our shield, dear, a heavy blow just for him, and a ring of fire left behind where it landed. Everyone else keeps out of the circle at his feet. He wanders off before it lands, and embers rain on us all after, a little each. Not yet!",
      bloodreaver: "A crown of embers for me! A good one! The others kept out of the circle at my feet. A ring of fire stayed where it landed, so I walked off first. Embers fell on all of us after, a little each. Bleed first, then drink.",
      runeguard: "The omen: a crown of embers settles over the shield, and the circle at his feet is a warning for the rest. The answer: I take it, having walked off first, since a ring of fire remains where it lands; embers then fall on all of us, a little each. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "A crown of embers, served flaming to me alone: a rich, smoky dish. The others stayed clear of the circle at my feet. It left a ring of fire behind where it landed, so I carried the plate to an empty corner first. Embers then fell on every guest, a little each. Overcooked. Delicious.",
      oathbroker: "The crown is levied upon me alone, a heavy sum, and the others stay clear of the circle at my feet. The fine print: a ring of fire remains where it lands. I carried it away from the dance before it fell. Embers then fall on all the undersigned, a little each. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "A crown of embers came to me alone, a heavy word. The others stayed out of the circle at my feet. I walked away before it landed, so the ring of fire it left lay where we did not stand. Embers fell on all of us after, a little each. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Crown of embers on the shield-man. Heavy blow, circle at his feet, keep out of it. Ring of fire stays where it lands, so he walked it to the edge first. Kept to the far lane. Embers fall on everyone after, a little each. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "A crown of embers settled on our shield, which is vanity. The circle at his feet is for him alone. A ring of fire stays where it lands, so he walked it away first, and I kept off the burnt floor. Embers rained on us all, a little each. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "A crown of embers on our shield, all gold and furious, and I admit I was jealous! Everyone else kept out of the circle at his feet. The ring of fire it leaves stays, so he carried it off first. Embers fell on all of us after, a little each. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Cold read: a crown of embers over our shield, a circle at his feet, a ring of fire left behind. Keep out, and walk it away from the floor we need. Hot read: embers fall on everyone after, a little each. Back to the middle, past the ring.",
      driftblade: "A crown of embers closed round our shield and the rest of us ran clear of the circle at his feet, and the ring of fire it left stayed where it landed, so I ran round it, through the gaps, never once still in it, though embers fell on us all after, a little each.",
      alembist: "Ailment: a crown of embers on the shield, a circle at his feet, a ring of fire left where it lands. Remedy: the rest stay clear; the shield carries it to an empty corner before it lands. Note: embers fall on all after, a little each. Label: do not stand on the ring.",
      threadweaver: "A crown of embers over our knight, a heavy blow, and my stitches stayed out of the circle at his feet. A ring of fire stays where it lands, so he walked it away from the middle first. Embers fell on every stitch after, a little each. A neat seam. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "A crown of embers for our shield, a solo number. The company stayed out of the circle at his feet. A ring of fire stays where it lands, so he took it to a downstage corner, away from the blocking. (Spotlight, then smoke, then embers on the whole house, a little each.)",
      cleric: "A crown of embers for our knight, and a circle at his feet we kept out of. I laid the light on him before it landed. The ring of fire stayed where it fell, so he took it somewhere harmless, and embers fell on us all after, a little each. Dawn keep him.",
      grovekeeper: "A crown of embers on the knight, heavy as a late frost. We stayed out of the circle at his feet, and I had planted on him before. The ring of fire stays where it lands, so he walked it away first. Embers fell on all my lot after, a little each. Plant first.",
      chronomancer: "The crown falls a beat after the circle locks. The knight walked it away from the floor we needed, and I mended him early. The ring of fire stayed behind, and embers fell on us all a beat after, a little each. I did.",
      tidecaller: "A crown of embers for our knight, a heavy surge, and a circle at his feet we kept out of. I let the water rise on him first. A ring of fire stays where it lands, so he walked the tide away. Embers fell on us all after, a little each. Mind the tide.",
      lanternkeeper: "A crown of embers fell on our knight alone. I hung a light on him before it landed and we kept out of the circle at his feet. A ring of fire stays where it lands, so he walked it away first. Embers fell on every one of us after, a little each.",
      kenseier: "The crown is aimed at me. It has a count, and I took it at the landing with ash about me; the rest stayed out of the circle at my feet. The ring of fire stays behind, so I walked it away. Embers then fell on us all, a little each. Breathe, then strike.",
      houndmaster: "Crown of embers on the shield-man. Heavy blow, circle at his feet. Dogs and I kept out of it. Ring of fire stays where it lands, so he walked the big lad's gift to a far corner first. Embers fell on the lot of us after, a little each. Sit. Good dogs.",
    } },
    'Pinning Thrust': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "He lunged at me down a line, and the line locked on me late. It drives me to the wall along it, and anything solid behind me adds a heavy slam. I put the open floor behind me and the star out of the line. The rest kept off it. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "A lunge down a line from him through me, and it drove me to the wall. Anything solid behind me adds a slam, so I made sure the line ran over bare floor. The rest stayed off it. Pinned to a wall is a position I know well.",
      thresher: "He lunges at our shield, dear, down a straight line, and carries him all the way to the wall. Nothing solid must lie behind the poor man, or it hurts him twice. So he turns the line to open floor first, and the rest of us keep off it. Off we go.",
      bloodreaver: "A lunge down a line, right through me, and it shoved me to the wall like a drunk to a doorway! Anything solid behind me would have made it hurt more, so I put the line over open floor first. The others kept off it. A good one.",
      runeguard: "The omen: a lunge down a line from his feet through me, locking late. The answer: it drives me to the wall along it, and anything solid in the way adds a slam, so I place the line across open floor. The rest keep off it. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "A lunge from my host, straight down a line through me, and I was carried to the wall like a plate on a trolley. Anything solid behind me would have bruised the dish, so I put the line over open floor. The others kept off the line. Cold.",
      oathbroker: "The thrust is served down a line, through me, and I am carried to the wall along it. The fine print: anything solid lying behind me is a penalty. I place the line across open floor. The others remain off the line. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "He spoke to me down a long line, a lunge that carries me to the wall. Anything solid behind me would make it a harder word. I turned him so the line ran over open floor, and the others stayed off it. Then I answered. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Lunge down a line through the shield-man. Drives him to the wall. Solid thing behind him, he takes a slam. He put the line across open floor. Rest kept off the line. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "He lunged at our shield down a line, which is showing off, and drove him to the wall. A solid thing behind him would have hurt more, so he turned the mark till the line crossed bare floor. I kept off it. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "A lunge down a line through our knight, and he was driven to the wall like a cork! Something solid in the way would have made it far worse, so he aimed the line at bare floor first. The rest of us kept off the line. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Cold read: a lunge down a line through our shield, locking late, and it drives him to the wall. Anything solid behind him is a slam. Hot read: I did not want to be anywhere near that line. Back to the middle, off it.",
      driftblade: "He lunged down a line through our knight and drove him to the wall and anything solid in the way would have been a slam, so the knight turned the line over open floor and the rest of us ran round it, off it, never landing in its road.",
      alembist: "Ailment: a lunge down a line through the shield, ending at the wall. Remedy: aim the line at open floor, nothing solid behind him, the rest off the line. Note: the star is solid. Label: mind what is at the end.",
      threadweaver: "He drove our knight to the wall down a straight line, like a pin through cloth. Anything solid behind him would have made it two blows, so he turned the line to bare floor first and the rest of my stitches kept off it. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "A lunge down a line through our shield, driven to the wings with a crash. Anything solid in the way adds a second crash, so he put the line across an empty stage. The company kept off it. (Exit, the shield, with force.)",
      cleric: "A lunge down a line at our knight, driving him to the wall. Anything solid behind him would have hurt him twice, so he put the line over open floor, and the rest of us kept off it. I mended him as he landed. Dawn keep him.",
      grovekeeper: "He drove our knight to the wall like a gale pushing a tree over. Anything solid in the way adds a second blow, so the knight turned the line across open floor and the rest of my lot kept off it. Plant first, and read the wind.",
      chronomancer: "The line is drawn a beat before the lunge, and locks late. It drives the knight to the wall, and anything solid behind him adds a second blow. He put the line on open floor, the rest stayed off it. I'll have said so. I did.",
      tidecaller: "A lunge down a line at our knight, like a wave running up a shore, and it carried him to the wall. Anything solid behind him would have hurt twice, so he turned the line to open floor. The rest of us stayed out of the current. Mind the tide.",
      lanternkeeper: "He lunged down a line through our knight and drove him to the wall. I lit the open floor at the end of the line and he turned till it was there; nothing solid behind him. The rest of us kept off it. One lamp, one line.",
      kenseier: "A lunge down a line, aimed at me, and the line locks late. I met it as it landed and was driven to the wall along it. Anything solid in the way adds a slam, so I turned the line over open floor first. The rest stayed off it. Catch the beat.",
      houndmaster: "Lunge at the shield-man down a line, drove him to the wall. Solid thing behind him, he'd take a slam on top, so he put the line over bare floor. Dogs and I kept off the road. Like a bull at a gate. Heel.",
    } },
    'Grace Withdrawn': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "His grace left us all. Everyone was left on the last thread, and none of it was a blow. Nothing hit us while we stood at nothing. We stood close to the healer, kept out of everything, and got mended for what came next. Held, barely.",
      gloomsworn: "He lifted his grace off every one of us, and left us on the last thread. Nothing struck. I know what it is to be at nothing and still standing. We stayed close to the healer and kept out of everything until we were mended.",
      thresher: "He withdrew his grace, dear, and left every one of us on the last thread, but no blow came with it. The trick is to stay out of everything and get mended at once, for the dark follows. Do mind the step, all of you. In time!",
      bloodreaver: "He took my wounds and everyone's, all at once, and left us at nothing! Nothing hit us. That is a hard thing to love. Stay out of everything, get close to the healer, and be mended before what follows. A fine scar, barely.",
      runeguard: "The omen: his grace is withdrawn, and every one of us is left on the last thread of life. Nothing strikes. The answer: stand clear of everything, gather near the healer, and be mended before the dark that follows. Not foreseen at first; now it is.",
      gorgemaw: "My host took everyone's plate away and left us at the very last crumb. Nothing struck. We kept out of everything and gathered near the healer to be refilled before the next course arrived. A cruel little amuse-bouche. Still hungry.",
      oathbroker: "His grace is withdrawn and the whole party is left on the last thread, but no blow attaches. The clause: stay clear of every other danger, gather near the healer, and be mended before the second instalment falls due. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "He took his grace from every one of us. No blow, only silence, and each of us on the last thread. We stayed out of everything and gathered close to the healer, and breathed until we were mended. Then it came. Breathe.",
      ranger: "His grace gone. Everyone on the last thread. Nothing struck. Kept out of everything, closed up near the healer, got mended before the next. Worst moment to take one more step wrong. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "He withdrew his grace from us all, which is a poor way to treat a guest, and left every one of us on the last thread. Nothing struck. I stood near the healer, off everything, and waited to be mended. It never saw me flinch.",
      pyromancer: "He took his grace away and left every one of us on the last thread, glowing the colour of dread! Nothing struck, but I stood very still near the healer, out of every fire, and was mended before what followed. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Cold read: his grace withdrawn, everyone on the last thread, no blow. Stay out of everything. Gather near the healer. Hot read: my heart ran hot with fright. Steadied. Mended. Back to the middle, before the next.",
      driftblade: "He took his grace from us all and left every one of us on the last thread and nothing hit, so I did not run, which I hate, and stayed close to the healer and off everything while the mending came, and then the dark followed.",
      alembist: "Ailment: grace withdrawn; every one of us on the last thread, no blow. Remedy: stay out of everything, gather near the healer, be mended before what follows. Note: brew before it, not after, and bring the big flask. Label: nobody dies of this one.",
      threadweaver: "He pulled every thread in the party down to the last, and left each of us on the last thread of life. No blow came with it. I drew my stitches in close, kept them out of everything, and mended before what followed. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "Act break! The whole company left on the last thread of life by his sudden hush, and no blow. We stood close to the healer, off every mark, and were mended in the wings before the next. (Hold. Hold. Applause, quietly.)",
      cleric: "He took his grace from every one of us and left us on the last thread, with no blow at all. I gathered my dears close and mended them quickly, and we kept out of everything. It is a frightening gift. Dawn keep us.",
      grovekeeper: "It felt like a drought taking every root in the field at once: everyone left on the last thread, and no blow. We stayed close to me and out of everything, and I planted the cure fast, before what followed. Plant first.",
      chronomancer: "He takes everything back at once, and I will have been ready. Everyone on the last thread, no blow, and what follows comes a few beats after. We stayed close to the healer, out of everything, and were mended before the second. Well. Almost.",
      tidecaller: "He drew all the water out of us at once, a tide run to the very mud: everyone on the last thread, no blow. We stood close, out of everything, and I let the water rise again before what followed. There was no hurry. There never is. Mind the tide.",
      lanternkeeper: "All our lights went down to the last glimmer, no blow at all. I gathered the party close, kept them out of everything, and lit every wick again before what followed. A light for each of us, quickly. I'll leave one burning.",
      kenseier: "A blow with no beat and nothing to turn: his grace withdrawn, and every one of us left on the last thread. We stayed out of everything and drew in close to the healer, and were mended. Some blows are only outlasted. Ash settles.",
      houndmaster: "He took everybody's strength at a stroke, dogs too, all on the last thread, and no blow. Kept out of everything, called the dogs in tight beside the healer, got mended. Easy, lads. Good dogs.",
    } },
    'Nightfall': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Nightfall reached every one of us a few heartbeats after the grace left. Nothing to block, and we were at nothing when it came, so the healer had to have us all up first. We stood close and took it. Held, barely.",
      gloomsworn: "The dark came for every one of us soon after the grace left, and we had to be mended before it landed. Nothing to hide behind. We stood close to the healer and took it. The watch has seen worse nights.",
      thresher: "Nightfall reaches every one of us, dear, a few heartbeats after the grace is gone, so mend everyone up, every last one, before it lands. Stay close to the healer and don't wander. It is the whole point of the evening. Off we go.",
      bloodreaver: "The dark hit every one of us a heartbeat after the grace was gone! If you aren't mended by then, you fall. The healer filled us all up, quick, and we took it together. The hardest blow in the world, and I was glad of it. A fine scar.",
      runeguard: "The omen: the grace goes, and a moment later Nightfall reaches every one of us. The answer: be mended in full before it lands, gather close to the healer, and let nothing else touch us meanwhile. As foreseen, and heavy.",
      gorgemaw: "Nightfall, a dark course for the whole table at once, served a few heartbeats after the plates were cleared. Everyone must be filled to the brim before it lands, close to the healer. A cruel thing, to starve a party and then feed it a banquet.",
      oathbroker: "Nightfall falls due upon all parties a few heartbeats after the grace is withdrawn. The clause: every one of the undersigned must be mended in full beforehand, gathered near the healer, or default is certain. The hardest clause in the realm. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "The dark spoke to all of us at once, soon after the grace left. We stood close together, mended in full before it came, and took it as one. I listened until it passed. Then we answered. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Nightfall. Hits everyone a few heartbeats after the grace goes. Need the healer to get everyone full first. Closed up and stood still. No lane to take. Clean line, barely.",
      shadowblade: "Nightfall reached every one of us, and there was no shadow to hide in, which was rude of it. The healer had to top us all up in the heartbeats after the grace left. I stood close to her and waited. It never saw me, but it found me.",
      pyromancer: "Nightfall! It hit every one of us, a few heartbeats after the grace left, and I stood very close to the healer and was mended in full in the nick of time. I held my breath the whole while. Only my sleeve smouldered.",
      thermist: "Cold read: Nightfall, a few heartbeats after the grace, on everyone. Be mended in full before it lands. Close to the healer. Hot read: I ran hot with fright waiting for it. Steadied. Back to the middle, together.",
      driftblade: "Nightfall reached everyone a few heartbeats after the grace left and there was nowhere to run so I ran in to the healer instead, through the others, and was mended and stood close and took it with them, never once wanting to leave.",
      alembist: "Ailment: Nightfall, on everyone, a few heartbeats after grace is withdrawn. Remedy: mend all of us in full beforehand, gathered close to the healer. Note: brew before it, not after. Label: the hardest dose on the shelf.",
      threadweaver: "Nightfall reached every thread at once, a few heartbeats after the grace was gone. I drew my stitches in close, mended every one in full before it landed, and let it run through us together. The hardest seam of my life. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "Nightfall, the second half of the curtain: it fell on the whole house a few heartbeats after the hush. The company gathered near the healer, mended in full beforehand, and took it together. (A standing ovation. For the healer.)",
      cleric: "Nightfall reached every one of us a few heartbeats after the grace left. I gathered my dears close so one prayer could reach them all, and mended every one in full before it fell. Thank the light I was quick.",
      grovekeeper: "Nightfall came like a hard frost after a still evening, on every one of us. I gathered my lot close and planted the cure on every one before it broke, since a late mend is no mend. Plant first, always. The surest rule I know.",
      chronomancer: "Nightfall reaches everyone a beat or two after the grace goes, and I will have mended all of them by then. We stood close to the healer for it. The hardest beat of the fight, and I kept it. I did.",
      tidecaller: "Nightfall broke over every one of us soon after the grace left, like the last wave of a storm tide. I let the water rise on all of them at once, so it was high when the dark came. Close together, no hurry. Wait for the water.",
      lanternkeeper: "Nightfall reached every one of us soon after the grace left. I lit every wick again, all at once, before it came, and the party stood close to my lamp. A light for each of us. Keep your light.",
      kenseier: "Nightfall has no beat a blade can turn: it reaches everyone soon after the grace leaves. We drew in close to the healer and were mended in full beforehand, and outlasted it. Breathe, then strike.",
      houndmaster: "Nightfall hit the lot of us soon after he took the strength, dogs too. Healer had to fill us all up first, so we stood in tight beside her. Easy, lads. Took it together. Good dogs.",
    } },
    'Starfall': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Shards broke off the meteor and blue rings opened on the floor, only inside the shadow. One of us stood in each, and a rain reached all of us after. The ring wants one body, no more. I took mine and the healer topped us up. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "Blue rings opened inside the shadow where the shards were falling, and each wanted one of us standing in it. A rain on everyone followed. I took a ring; the dead don't mind a falling star. The healer saw to the rain.",
      thresher: "Blue rings open on the floor inside the shadow, dear, where the star-shards will fall, and one of us stands in each. Then a rain reaches everybody, so be mended. Do walk in when the shards show. It is only a small appointment. Not yet!",
      bloodreaver: "Chunks of the sky came down, and blue rings opened inside the shadow, one friend in each! A rain on everyone followed. I took a ring and the whole falling star with it. It hurt just right. Keep out of the rest, and be mended for the rain.",
      runeguard: "The omen: shards break off the meteor, and blue rings open inside its shadow. The answer: one of us stands in each ring, no more are needed, and the healer mends all for the rain that follows. Always inside the shadow, never outside. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "The sky served shards, and blue rings opened inside the shadow like places laid at the table, one for each guest willing to sit. A rain of the same stuff fell on everyone after. I took my seat. Crunchy. Still hungry.",
      oathbroker: "Blue rings were entered inside the shadow, each requiring one of the undersigned to stand in it and take the shard. The fine print: nobody stands in a ring unfilled, and a rain falls upon all parties afterward. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "Shards fell as blue rings inside the shadow, a word for one voice each. I stood in mine and took it. Then the rain spoke to all of us at once, and we were mended for it. Then we answered. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Shards from the meteor. Blue rings inside the shadow only. One of us in each, no more needed. Rain on everyone after. Took the nearest ring and got mended. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "Shards fell as blue rings, only inside the shadow, and each wanted one of us standing in it, which is a poor use of a shadow. I took one. A rain on everyone followed, and I stood near the healer. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "Chunks of the sky fell, and blue rings opened inside the shadow, one of us in each! I stepped into mine with great dignity and took the lot. The rain on everyone after was the part that singed. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Cold read: blue rings inside the shadow, where the shards fall. One of us stands in each. Rain on everyone after. Hot read: it was glorious to be hit by something so bright. Be mended. Back to the middle.",
      driftblade: "Shards broke off the meteor and blue rings opened inside the shadow and I ran to the nearest one, through the others, and stood in it just long enough, the only time I stand at all, and then the rain came on everyone and I never landed.",
      alembist: "Ailment: shards from the meteor; blue rings inside the shadow, each needing one of us standing in it. Remedy: one body per ring, then mending for the rain that follows. Note: the rain is for all. Label: bright, brief, bruising.",
      threadweaver: "Blue rings opened inside the shadow where the shards were falling, one of my stitches in each. A rain reached the whole hem after. I counted who was nearest to which ring and sent them in, and mended after. A neat seam. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "Blue rings lit on the floor inside the shadow, spotlights for a single player each. A shard fell on each. The company chose who stood where, and the rain after fell on everyone. (Each player to a light, one to a light.)",
      cleric: "Shards broke off the meteor and blue rings opened inside the shadow, and one of my dears stood in each. A rain on all of us followed. I mended them before and after, since the rain reaches everyone. Dawn keep us.",
      grovekeeper: "Shards fell like hail in one place at a time, blue rings inside the shadow, and one of my lot stood in each. A rain fell on everyone after. I planted the cure early, since hail is quick. Plant first.",
      chronomancer: "The blue rings come first and the shards a beat after, inside the shadow, one of us in each. The rain on everyone follows the shards. I mended early, and will have mended again. We were never idle.",
      tidecaller: "Shards fell like spray from a great wave, and blue rings opened inside the shadow, one of us in each. The rain came on all of us after. I let the water rise early so it was high when the rain broke. Mind the tide.",
      lanternkeeper: "Blue rings opened inside the shadow where the shards would fall, and one of us stood in each. I hung a light at the edge of each ring so they knew where to walk. A rain reached everyone after, and I topped up every wick. Keep your light.",
      kenseier: "The shards have a beat: the blue rings open, the shard falls, the rain follows. One of us stood in each ring and took the shard. A blade cannot turn a falling star. The rain on everyone is only outlasted. Breathe, then strike.",
      houndmaster: "Pieces of the sky came down. Blue rings inside the shadow, one of us in each, dogs kept out. Rain on the lot of us after. Healer topped us up. Like standing under a bull's belly, only bright. Heel.",
    } },
    'The Starwyrm': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "He lifted his blade and the stars above us knotted into a serpent, which coiled round the room near the wall, a red band moving as it passed. We kept in toward the star, off the rim, and held the middle. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "He lifted his blade and the stars came loose, and knotted into a serpent that coiled round the room near the wall. Its path was painted red. We kept in toward the star until it passed. The wall is a poor place to stand.",
      thresher: "Up goes his blade, dear, and the stars knot themselves into a serpent, which coils all the way round the room near the wall! Its road is painted red. Keep toward the star, away from the rim, and let it pass. Do mind the step. Off we go.",
      bloodreaver: "He raised his blade and the stars knotted into a great snake that coiled round the room near the wall! The path was painted red as it moved. We kept in toward the star, off the rim. A fine monster. I'd have wrestled it if the red allowed.",
      runeguard: "The omen: his blade rises and the constellations knot into a serpent. The answer: it coils round the room near the wall, a red band painted as it passes, so we keep in toward the star and off the rim until it has gone. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "My host raised his blade and the stars knotted into a serpent, a long, coiling course served round the rim of the table. Its road was painted red. We kept in toward the centre, off the edge, and let it slide past. Cold, and far too long.",
      oathbroker: "Upon his signal the constellations are bound into a serpent, and it coils about the room near the wall. The fine print: its passage is painted red, and the rim is forfeit. The undersigned remain toward the centre. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "He lifted his blade and the stars joined into a serpent. It coiled round the room near the wall, a long word spoken in red. We kept toward the star, away from the rim, and listened until it passed. Then we answered. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Blade up. Stars knot into a serpent. It coils round the room near the wall, path painted red as it goes. Kept toward the star, off the rim. It passed. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "He raised his blade and the stars knotted into a serpent, which is a dramatic way to spend an evening. It coiled round the room near the wall, the path painted red. I kept toward the star, off the rim. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "He raised his blade and the stars knotted into a serpent, all light and teeth, and it coiled round the room near the wall in a red band! I kept toward the star, away from the rim, and admired it. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Cold read: blade up, stars knot into a serpent, it coils round the room near the wall in a red band. Keep in toward the star. Hot read: the rim looked inviting. Too far. Back to the middle, where it isn't.",
      driftblade: "He lifted his blade and the stars knotted into a serpent that coiled round the room near the wall in a moving red band, and I kept toward the star and circled it, never going near the rim, and watched the serpent slide past.",
      alembist: "Ailment: a serpent of stars, coiling round the room near the wall in a red band. Remedy: keep toward the star, off the rim, until it passes. Note: it takes a full round. Label: stay inside the circle it draws.",
      threadweaver: "He raised his blade and the stars knotted into a serpent, which coiled round the room near the wall, a red band laid out like a long seam. We stayed toward the star, inside it, and let it close its stitch. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "Our leading man raised his blade and the constellations knotted into a serpent that coiled round the stage along the wall, painted red as it passed. The company kept toward the centre, off the edge. (The serpent, upstage, going round.)",
      cleric: "He raised his blade and the stars knotted into a serpent, which coiled round the room near the wall in a red band. I called my dears in toward the star, away from the rim, until it had passed. Dawn keep us.",
      grovekeeper: "He lifted his blade and the stars knotted into a serpent like a great vine round the room near the wall, painted red as it grew. My lot kept in toward the star, off the rim. The rim is where vines go. Plant first.",
      chronomancer: "The serpent coils round the room near the wall, a red band that lands a beat behind its head. We kept in toward the star, off the rim, and let it pass. I'll have told them to. I did.",
      tidecaller: "He raised his blade and the stars knotted into a serpent, which coiled round the room near the wall like a tide running along a shore, painted red as it came. We kept toward the star and off the rim. Wait for the water.",
      lanternkeeper: "The stars knotted into a serpent when he raised his blade, and it coiled round the room near the wall in a red band. I lit the ground toward the star and we all stood there, off the rim, till it had passed. A light for each of us.",
      kenseier: "He raised his blade, the stars joined into a serpent, and it coiled round the room near the wall. No beat to turn: a red band to read and avoid. We kept toward the star, off the rim. Honest, for a serpent. Breathe, then strike.",
      houndmaster: "He raised his blade and the stars knotted into a big snake that coiled round the room by the wall, red path painted behind it. Kept the dogs and myself toward the star, off the rim. Sit. Let it slither past. Heel.",
    } },
    'Embers of Heaven': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Embers fell on some of the shards round the star, red circles round those shards, and they broke. What was left of them and the star was all the shelter we had. We kept out of the circles and marked which shards would stand. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "Embers fell on some of the shards round the star, painted red, and they broke. We kept out of the circles and looked at what was left standing. That was the cover we had to hide behind. I have hidden behind less.",
      thresher: "Embers drop on a few of the star's shards, dear, with red circles round those shards, and they break. Keep out of the circles and mind what is left, for that is the shelter you will have. A tidy little demolition. Off we go.",
      bloodreaver: "Embers came down on some of the shards, red circles round them, and they cracked apart! Stay out of the circles and notice which shards remain, because the ones left are the only cover. I'll shelter behind anything. Anything.",
      runeguard: "The omen: embers fall upon some of the shards round the star, a red circle round each. The answer: stand clear of the circles and note which shards will remain, for those and the star are the only cover. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "Embers dropped like cinders onto a few of the star's shards, red circles round them, and the shards crumbled. We stayed out of the circles and took note of what stood. That would be the only shelter for the next course. Crumbly.",
      oathbroker: "Embers are entered against some of the shards, a red circle round each, and those shards are forfeit. The undersigned stay clear of the circles and record which shards remain, for those and the star are the only cover. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "Embers fell on some of the shards, red circles round them, a short hard word each. They broke. We stayed out of the circles and marked what stood. Those would be our shelter. Then we answered. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Embers on some of the shards. Red circles round them. They break. Kept out. Noted which shards were left; those and the star are the only cover. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "Embers dropped on a few of the shards, red circles round them, and they broke, which is vandalism. I kept out of the circles and marked which shards would stand. Those were the shadows I had left to hide in. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "Embers fell on a few of the star's shards, red circles round each, and they burst in a lovely shower! I stayed out of the circles and took careful note of which shards were left. Mostly unsinged, and well informed.",
      thermist: "Cold read: embers on some of the shards, red circles round each. Stay out. Note which shards remain. Hot read: they burst gloriously. The shards and the star are the only cover. Back to the middle, and behind them.",
      driftblade: "Embers fell on some of the shards, red circles round them, and I went round and out of every circle and through the shards left standing, because what was left was the only cover, and I was learning where it stood, never landing.",
      alembist: "Ailment: embers on some of the shards, red circles round each. Remedy: stay out of the circles; note which shards remain, since those and the star are the only cover. Note: the shelter changes shape. Label: count what is left.",
      threadweaver: "Embers fell on some of the shards, a red circle round each, and they broke like pins snapped in a cushion. We kept out of the circles and marked which shards were left. Those and the star would be our shelter. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "Embers on some of the shards, a red circle round each: set pieces struck from the stage. The company kept out of the circles and noted which pieces stood. Those and the star were the only cover. (Exit, the scenery.)",
      cleric: "Embers fell on a few of the shards, red circles round them, and the shards broke. I kept my dears out of the circles and told them to remember which stood. Those and the star would be our only shelter. Dawn keep us.",
      grovekeeper: "Embers dropped on a few of the shards like sparks on dry grass, red circles round them, and they broke. We stayed out of the circles and marked which stood. Those and the star would be our shelter. Plant first, and pick your hedge.",
      chronomancer: "The embers land a beat after the circles, on a few of the shards, and the shards break. We kept out of the circles and noted which stood. Those and the star would be the only cover, and I'll have remembered which. I did.",
      tidecaller: "Embers fell on a few of the shards like rain on a reef, red circles round each, and they broke. We stood out of the circles and marked what remained, for those and the star were the only cover. Wait for the water.",
      lanternkeeper: "Embers fell on some of the shards, a red circle round each. I stayed out of the circles and made note of which shards were left standing, because those and the star were the only shelter. A light for each of us. I'll leave one burning.",
      kenseier: "Embers on some of the shards, a red circle round each, with a count to the landing. The shards broke. We stayed out of the circles and marked what stood. A blade cannot be a shelter; the star and what remains must be. Catch the beat.",
      houndmaster: "Embers dropped on a few shards, red circles round them. Broke the lot. Kept dogs and myself out of the circles and noted what was left. That and the star are the only cover. Easy, lads. Heel.",
    } },
    'Constellation Fall': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The serpent reared on the rim and breathed starlight across the whole floor. Only the star's shadow was safe. We stood behind it, with the star between us and the serpent, and the shield-man held him there too. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "The serpent reared on the rim and breathed starlight over the whole floor, and only the shadow behind the star was spared. We stood in it, with the star between us and the breath. Even I hide from some things.",
      thresher: "The serpent rears on the rim, dear, and breathes starlight across the whole floor, and nothing is safe but the star's own shadow. Get behind the star, with it between you and the serpent. Do mind that the shards left standing help. Off we go.",
      bloodreaver: "The snake reared and breathed starlight over the whole floor! It hits too hard to love. The only ground it can't touch is behind the star, with the star between us and the serpent. I hid, which I rarely do. A fine scar, avoided.",
      runeguard: "The omen: the serpent rears on the rim, and the light gathers. The answer: the breath covers the whole floor but the star's shadow, so stand behind the star or a shard that remains, with it between us and the serpent. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "The serpent reared on the rim and breathed a banquet of starlight across the whole floor. Only the star's shadow was spared. We sat behind the star, with it between us and the serpent. Nearly all of it was too rich to survive.",
      oathbroker: "The serpent rears and breathes upon the whole floor. The fine print: only the shadow of the star is exempt. The undersigned stand behind the star, or a shard that remains, with it between us and the serpent. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "The serpent reared and spoke over the whole floor in starlight. Only the shadow behind the star was silent. We stood in it, the star between us and the serpent, and listened until it passed. Then we answered. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Serpent rears on the rim. Breathes starlight over the whole floor. Only the star's shadow is safe. Got behind the star, star between us and the serpent. Watched where it reared first. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The serpent reared on the rim and lit the whole floor with starlight, leaving no shadow anywhere but behind the star. I took it, with the star between me and the serpent. It was the only dark worth having. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "The serpent reared and breathed a flood of starlight across the whole floor, and nowhere was safe but the star's shadow! I got behind the star, with it between me and the serpent, and it was dazzling. Mostly unsinged, and thrilled.",
      thermist: "Cold read: the serpent rears on the rim, starlight across the whole floor. Only the star's shadow is spared. Behind the star, star between us and the serpent. Hot read: I could feel it on my back. Back to the middle, behind the star.",
      driftblade: "The serpent reared on the rim and breathed starlight across the whole floor and I ran round the star, through the others, to the far side of it, with the star between us, and stood still for once, which I hate, and was spared.",
      alembist: "Ailment: starlight across the whole floor from a serpent reared on the rim. Remedy: stand behind the star or a shard that remains, with it between you and the serpent. Note: watch where it rears first. Label: hide fast.",
      threadweaver: "The serpent reared on the rim and breathed starlight across the whole floor like a sheet pulled taut, and only the star's shadow was spared. I drew every stitch in behind it, the star between us and the serpent. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "The serpent reared upstage and washed the whole house in starlight, all but the star's shadow. The company took the wings behind the star, with it between us and the serpent. (The scenery, doing its one job.)",
      cleric: "The serpent reared on the rim and breathed starlight over the whole floor, and only the shadow behind the star was spared. I gathered my dears there, the star between us and the serpent. Thank the light for solid things.",
      grovekeeper: "The serpent reared and breathed starlight across the whole floor like a wildfire over a field. Only the lee of the star was spared. We stood behind it, the star between us and the serpent. Every storm has a lee. Plant first.",
      chronomancer: "The serpent rears on the rim, and a beat later the starlight covers the whole floor. Only the star's shadow is spared. We got behind the star, with it between us and the serpent, before the beat. I'll have been behind it first.",
      tidecaller: "The serpent reared on the rim and breathed starlight over the whole floor like a wave that covers the beach to the dunes, and only the lee of the star was spared. We stood behind it. There was no hurry, but there was a place. Mind the tide.",
      lanternkeeper: "The serpent reared on the rim and breathed starlight across the whole floor, and only the shadow behind the star was spared. I lit that place and we all stood in it, the star between us and the serpent. A light for each of us.",
      kenseier: "A breath of starlight over the whole floor: no beat to turn, no blade that can meet it. Only the star's shadow was spared. We stood behind it, with the star between us and the serpent, and outlasted it. Ash settles.",
      houndmaster: "Big snake reared on the rim and breathed light over the whole floor. Only the star's shadow was safe. Stood the lot of us behind the star, dogs tight, the star between us and the beast. Like standing behind a barn in a gale. Heel.",
    } },
    'Ascendant': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "The crater fell away to a floor of cloud above the falling meteor, and the star was gone with it. No cover now, and the room smaller. The Wake gained an inner ring after the outer. Read all of it. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "The crater fell away and left us on cloud above the burning meteor, the star and its shards gone. He climbed where we could not strike. After that the Wake had an inner ring, numbered after the outer. I have fallen further than this.",
      thresher: "The crater falls away, dear, and we stand on a circle of cloud above the falling meteor, with no star to hide behind. He cannot be struck while he climbs. After that the Wake has an inner ring, last in the order. Do mind the step. Off we go.",
      bloodreaver: "The crater fell away and we stood on cloud above the burning rock! No star to hide behind, a smaller room, and he out of reach as he climbed. Then the Wake got a second ring, inside the first, numbered last. A grander floor for a grander scar.",
      runeguard: "The omen: the crater falls away, and the floor becomes cloud above the falling meteor. The answer: no cover remains, the room is smaller, and the Wake gains an inner ring numbered after the outer. Read the whole order. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "My host changed the dining room mid-meal: the crater fell away and we stood on cloud above the falling meteor, no star left to eat behind. The Wake gained an inner ring after the outer, a second helping. Read it all. Rich.",
      oathbroker: "The premises were exchanged mid-contract: the crater falls away and we stand on cloud above the meteor. No cover remains, and the Wake gains an inner ring numbered after the outer. The undersigned read the whole schedule. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "The crater fell away, and we stood on cloud over the burning rock. He rose where we could not answer. The Wake gained a second ring inside the first, numbered after it. I read the whole sentence before I moved. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Crater drops away. Cloud floor above the meteor. No star, no cover. Smaller room. Wake gets an inner ring, numbered after the outer. Read all of it. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "The crater fell away and left us on cloud above the burning rock, with no star to hide behind and nowhere dark. He climbed beyond my reach, which was rude. The Wake grew a second ring inside the first, numbered last. It never saw me, but I read it.",
      pyromancer: "The crater fell away and we stood on a circle of cloud over the burning meteor, lit from underneath! No star to hide behind, a smaller room, and the Wake grew a second ring, inside the first, numbered last. Mostly unsinged, and thrilled.",
      thermist: "Cold read: crater gone, cloud floor above the meteor, no cover, a smaller room. The Wake gains an inner ring numbered after the outer. Hot read: the glow from below was fierce. Read it all. Back to the middle, carefully.",
      driftblade: "The crater fell away and we stood on cloud over the falling meteor, no star left to dodge round, a smaller room, and the Wake grew a second ring inside the first, numbered last, so I read both and went through the gaps of both, never landing.",
      alembist: "Ailment: the crater falls away; a cloud floor over the meteor; no cover; a smaller room. Remedy: the Wake now has an inner ring, numbered after the outer. Read it all. Note: nothing is solid but us. Label: the second form.",
      threadweaver: "The crater fell away and left us on a circle of cloud, no star to hide behind and less cloth to stand on. The Wake grew a second ring inside the first, numbered after it, like a second row of stitches. Read both. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "Act three! The crater fell away and the company stood on a circle of cloud above the falling meteor. No scenery to hide behind, a smaller stage. The Wake gained an inner ring, numbered after the outer. (Read the whole script.)",
      cleric: "The crater fell away and we stood on cloud above the burning meteor, with no star to shelter behind. He rose where we could not strike. After that the Wake had an inner ring, numbered after the outer. I told my dears to read it all. Dawn keep us.",
      grovekeeper: "The crater fell away, dear, and we stood on cloud above the burning meteor, like seedlings on a roof. No star to shelter behind, a smaller room, and the Wake grew a second ring inside the first, numbered last. Plant first, and read twice.",
      chronomancer: "The crater falls away, and the room becomes cloud above the falling meteor, with no star to shelter behind. The Wake gains a second ring inside the first, a few beats later in the order. I'll have read both already. I did.",
      tidecaller: "The crater fell away like an ebb tide, and we stood on a circle of cloud over the burning rock. No star to shelter behind. The Wake gained an inner ring, numbered after the outer, like a second wave behind the first. Mind the tide.",
      lanternkeeper: "The crater fell away and left us on cloud, lit from below by the falling meteor. No star to shelter behind, a smaller room. The Wake grew an inner ring numbered after the outer. I lit both rings in my head. Keep your light.",
      kenseier: "The crater fell away and we stood on cloud over the burning rock. He climbed, and cannot be struck while he climbs. The Wake gained an inner ring, numbered after the outer; the count simply goes on. Catch the beat.",
      houndmaster: "Crater fell away. Cloud floor over the burning rock, no star to stand behind, smaller room. Big lad climbed out of reach. The Wake got a second ring inside the first, numbered last. Read the lot, dogs at my heel. Heel.",
    } },
    'Horizon Cut': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "Shards fell on the whole room but one gap, a band of bare cloud across it. The gap moved every time. I found it as it opened and we filled it together before the shards landed. Sometimes a blue ring stood in the gap too; I took it, to catch the shard. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "Shards fell on the whole room but one gap between the red bands, and the gap moved each time. We found it and stood in it together. When a blue ring stood in the gap, I took it to catch the shard. I have never minded a narrow place.",
      thresher: "Shards rain on the whole room but one gap, dear, a quiet band between the red, it moves every time. Find it as it opens and all stand in it before the shards land. Sometimes a blue ring stands on the bare band and one of us steps in to catch a shard. Not yet!",
      bloodreaver: "The sky cut across the room and shards fell on all of it but one gap between the red! It moved every time. We found it and crowded in before the shards landed. Sometimes a blue ring sat in it, and I stood in that to catch the shard. A fine, tight squeeze.",
      runeguard: "The omen: the room is cut, red either side of one gap, shards on the red. The answer: find the gap as the cut is drawn, it moves, and have us all in it before they land; if a blue ring stands there, one of us takes it and catches the shard. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "My host cut the whole room across like a loaf, red on either side of one clean slice, and shards fell on the crusts. The gap moved each time. We all squeezed into the slice, and one of us sat in the blue ring there to catch the shard. A narrow dish. Tolerable.",
      oathbroker: "The room is cut across, and shards fall upon all of it but one gap between the red. The fine print: the gap moves every time. The undersigned stand in the gap before the shards land; when a blue ring stands there, one of us takes it and the shard, or all default. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "The room was cut across, with shards falling on all of it but one gap between the red. The gap moved each time. We found it as it opened and stood in it together. One of us stood in the blue ring there and caught the shard. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Room cut across. Red either side of one gap. Shards fall on the red. Gap moves every time. Found it early, everyone in it before the landing. Blue ring in the gap sometimes: one of us takes it, catches the shard. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "He cut the room across and left one gap, which is generous of him. Shards fell on the red either side. The gap moved each time, so I found it early and got everyone into it. Sometimes a blue ring sat in it, and someone caught the shard. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "He cut the whole room across, red on either side of a single gap, and shards fell on all of it but the gap! It moved every time. I found it quickly and we crowded in. When a blue ring sat there I stepped into it with dignity and caught the shard. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Cold read: the room cut across, red on both sides of one gap, shards on the red. Find the gap, all of us in it. Hot read: it moves, and sometimes a blue ring sits in it; one of us takes the ring and the shard. Back to the middle, which is the gap.",
      driftblade: "He cut the room across and left one gap between the red and the gap moved every time, so I ran for it when it opened, through the others, and pulled them into it with me, and when a blue ring sat there one of us ran into it and caught the shard.",
      alembist: "Ailment: shards on the whole room but one gap between the red. Remedy: find the gap, all of us in it before the landing. Note: the gap moves, and sometimes a blue ring sits in it; one of us catches the shard there. Label: look first, then step.",
      threadweaver: "He cut the room across like cloth and left one gap between the two red halves, and shards fell on both. The gap moved each time. I drew my stitches into it together, and one took the blue ring there to catch the shard. A tight hem. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "The stage was cut across, red on either side of one gap, shards falling on the red. The gap moved each time. The company crowded into it, and one player took the blue ring there to catch the shard. (A small spotlight, a large cast.)",
      cleric: "Such a lot of falling sky, and only one safe place in all of it, and it moved every time. I called my dears into it the moment it opened, and one stood in the blue ring there to catch the shard. Thank the light for a gap.",
      grovekeeper: "He cut the room across like a field under a plough, red on either side of one gap, and shards fell on the furrows. The gap moved every time. My lot crowded into it, and one stood in the blue ring there to catch the shard. Plant first.",
      chronomancer: "The gap opens a beat before the shards land, and it moves every time. We found it, all of us, and stood in it before the beat, and one of us took the blue ring there to catch the shard. I was.",
      tidecaller: "He cut the room across like a channel through shoals, red either side of one calm gap, shards on the shoals. The gap moved each time. We found the still water as it opened and stood in it together, and one took the blue ring there to catch the shard. Wait for the water.",
      lanternkeeper: "The room was cut across and shards fell on all of it but one gap between the red. The gap moved each time. I lit its middle as soon as it opened and we all stood in it together. When a blue ring stood there, one of us took it to catch the shard.",
      kenseier: "The room is cut across, red either side of one gap, and shards fall on the red. The gap moves every time. A cut I can read but not meet. We stood together in the gap, on the count, and one of us took the blue ring to catch the shard. Catch the beat.",
      houndmaster: "Room cut across, red either side of one gap, shards on the red. Gap moves every time. Whistled the dogs into it as it opened, the lot of us tight. Blue ring in it sometimes; one of us stood in it, caught the shard. Heel.",
    } },
    'The Sky Comes Down': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "He raised his blade and the whole sky came with it: the meteor, landing. There is no ground in the room that is spared. We did not hold it; we ended him first, the whole line at once. Held, only just.",
      gloomsworn: "He raised his blade and the meteor began to land, and nothing in the room is spared. There is nothing to hide behind. We ended him before it came. I know what it is to be out of time.",
      thresher: "He lifts his blade, dear, and the whole sky comes down with it, the meteor landing on everything. There is no spot to stand and no step to take. So we do not give him the hour. His name is on the list, and it is now. Not yet!",
      bloodreaver: "He ran out of patience and the whole sky came down with his blade, the meteor landing on everything! There is nowhere to stand. I hit him harder than I have ever hit anything, and so did we all. A glorious scar we did not get.",
      runeguard: "The omen: his blade rises and the sky descends with it, the meteor landing on everything. The answer: there is no ground spared, no cover, no step. He must fall before it lands. As foreseen, and written in haste.",
      gorgemaw: "My host rose to deliver his final course, and the whole sky came down with his blade. Not a corner of the table was spared. The only remedy is to finish the cook before the course arrives. We did, narrowly. Overcooked, and almost ours.",
      oathbroker: "The final instalment fell due: the sky comes down with his blade, and the meteor lands upon all parties. No ground is exempt. The only remedy is to conclude him before it lands. We did. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "He spoke his last word and the whole sky came down with it. No ground was spared. The only reply was to end him before the word was finished. We did. Then the quiet. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Blade up. Whole sky comes down. Meteor lands on everything. No cover, no lane. Only answer is to kill him first. Did. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "He raised his blade and the whole sky came down with it, which is the rudest thing he did. No shadow, no corner, no ground spared. The only answer was to kill the mark before it landed. It never saw me, nor the sky.",
      pyromancer: "He raised his blade and the whole sky came down with it, the meteor landing on everything! Nothing to stand behind, nothing to dodge, so I burned the biggest thing I have ever burned, and so did we all, before it landed. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Cold read: his blade rises, the whole sky comes down, the meteor lands on everything. No ground spared. Kill him first. Hot read: I have never burned so hard. Too far? Not tonight. Back to the middle, after.",
      driftblade: "He lifted his blade and the whole sky came down and there was nowhere to run and nothing to run through so I ran at him, through the others, and cut and cut and cut until he fell, before it landed, and never landed myself.",
      alembist: "Ailment: the whole sky, landing on everyone; no ground spared. Remedy: kill him before it lands. Note: there is no brew for this. Label: the last hurry. We made it, with our flasks nearly empty.",
      threadweaver: "He raised his blade and the whole sky came down with it, the meteor landing on every thread in the room. There is no seam to hide in. We cut him down before it landed, every one of us at once. Mind the slack, and the clock.",
      marionettist: "The finale! He raised his blade and the whole sky came down with it, the meteor landing on the entire house. No wings, no cover. The company ended him before the curtain fell. (A close call. Applause.)",
      cleric: "He raised his blade and the whole sky came down with it, the meteor landing on all of us. There is no ground spared and nothing to shelter behind. We ended him before it landed. I prayed through every blow. Dawn keep us.",
      grovekeeper: "He raised his blade and the whole sky came down with it, a frost and a flood at once, the meteor landing on everything. No ground is spared. There is nothing to plant against it. We ended him first. Plant first, and strike first.",
      chronomancer: "He raises his blade, and the sky lands a few beats later on everything. There is no ground spared. We ended him before the beats ran out. I will have known we would. I did not, but I will have.",
      tidecaller: "He raised his blade and the whole sky came down with it like a wave that has no shore to break on, the meteor landing on everything. Nothing to wait for now. We ended him before it came. The sea gives back, barely.",
      lanternkeeper: "He raised his blade and the whole sky came down with it, the meteor landing on everything. No ground was spared, nowhere to carry a lamp to. We ended him before it landed, all of us at once. Keep your light.",
      kenseier: "He raised his blade and the whole sky came down with it, a blow with no beat I could turn and no ground to stand on. The only answer was to end him before it landed. We did. The last honest stroke was ours. Ash settles.",
      houndmaster: "Raised his blade and the whole sky came down with it. Meteor landing on everything, dogs too. Nowhere to stand. Only way was to kill him first, so we did. Easy, lads. Good dogs.",
    } },
    'Mirrored Wake': { hard: true, learned: {
      bastion: "On the hard nights the dance runs twice, and the second pass is the first reflected across a line through the middle, with its own silver copies shown first. A spot that was clear the first time may be cut the second. I read it again, and moved. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "On the hard nights the dance comes twice. The second is the first mirrored across the middle, and he shows new silver copies before it. Ground that was safe once may be cut the second time. I do not trust a place because it lived once.",
      thresher: "On the hard nights, dear, the dance comes twice, the second a mirror of the first, with fresh silver copies shown before it begins. A spot that was safe the first time may be cut the second. Read the new copies and do mind the step. Off we go.",
      bloodreaver: "On the hard nights the dance came twice, the second a mirror of the first, with new silver copies shown before it started! A spot that was safe the first time got cut the second. I like a fight that answers back. A fine scar, avoided.",
      runeguard: "The omen, on the harder nights: the dance runs twice, the second pass the first reflected across a line through the middle, with fresh copies shown before it. The answer: read the new copies; the safe ground of the first may be cut in the second. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "On the hard nights my host served the dance twice, the second a mirror of the first, with fresh silver copies laid before it. A seat that was safe for the first course may be cut in the second. Read the new plates. Reheated, and reversed.",
      oathbroker: "On the harder terms the dance is performed twice, the second a mirror of the first, with fresh silver copies entered before it. The fine print: ground safe in the first pass may be cut in the second. We read the new copies. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "On hard nights the dance came twice. The second was the first spoken in a mirror, with new silver copies shown before it began. Ground that was safe once could be cut the second time. I read it again. Then we answered. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Hard nights: dance runs twice. Second pass is the first mirrored across the middle, new copies shown first. Safe ground the first time may be cut the second. Read again. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "On the hard nights he dances twice, the second a mirror of the first with fresh silver copies shown, which is vanity. Ground that was safe the first time can be cut the second. I read again before I moved. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "On the hard nights the dance came twice, the second a mirror of the first, with new silver copies glowing before it began! A spot that was safe the first time got cut the second. I read the copies again and moved, resentful. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Cold read: the dance comes twice, and the second pass is a mirror, with new copies shown before it. Ground that was safe may be cut. Hot read: I relaxed too soon, and felt it. Read again. Back to the middle, after the second pass.",
      driftblade: "On the hard nights the dance runs twice and the second is the first mirrored across the middle with new silver copies shown before it, so ground that was safe once might be cut the second time, and I read again and ran through, never landing twice.",
      alembist: "Ailment: on hard nights the dance runs twice; the second pass is the first reflected across the middle, with new silver copies. Remedy: read the second set afresh. Note: do not trust safe ground. Label: second dose, mirrored.",
      threadweaver: "On the hard nights he sews the seam twice, the second a mirror image of the first, with fresh silver copies pinned before it. Ground that was safe once may be cut the second time. Read the new pins. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "On the hard nights the dance is performed twice, the second a mirror of the first, with fresh silver copies taking their marks before it. (The blocking reversed. Read the marks again, company.) A safe spot may be cut in the encore.",
      cleric: "On the hard nights the dance comes twice, and the second is a mirror of the first, with new silver copies shown before it. Ground that was safe once may be cut the second time. I told my dears to read it again. Dawn keep us.",
      grovekeeper: "On the hard nights the dance comes twice, the second like the first seen in a pond, with new silver copies shown before it. A spot that was safe the first time may be cut the second. Read again. Plant first.",
      chronomancer: "On the hard nights the dance comes twice, the second a mirror of the first, with fresh silver copies shown before it, so the tune plays backwards. A safe spot may be cut the second time. I'll have read it twice. I did.",
      tidecaller: "On the hard nights the dance comes twice, the second a reflection of the first on still water, with new silver copies shown before it. A spot that was safe once may be cut the second time. Read the new water. Mind the tide.",
      lanternkeeper: "On the hard nights the dance comes twice, the second a mirror of the first, with fresh silver copies shown before it. Ground that was safe once may be cut the second time, so I lit it fresh. A light for each of us. I'll leave one burning.",
      kenseier: "On the hard nights the dance is played twice, the second a mirror of the first, with fresh silver copies shown before it. The count starts again. Ground that was safe once may be cut the second time. Catch the beat.",
      houndmaster: "Hard nights, the dance runs twice. Second's the first mirrored across the middle, new copies shown first. Safe spot the first time may be cut the second. Read it again, dogs at heel. Like walking a dog round a post twice. Heel.",
    } },
    'Second Coil': { hard: true, learned: {
      bastion: "On the hard nights the serpent came back and dived across the room along a painted line, a broad one. Nothing to hold, nothing to block. We stood either side of the line, not in it, and let it pass. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "On the hard nights the serpent returned and dived across the room along a painted line, broad as a grave. We stood well to either side of it and let it pass overhead. I have been under worse.",
      thresher: "On the hard nights the serpent comes back, dear, and dives across the room along a painted line, a broad one. Stand well to either side of the line, never in it, and let it pass. Do mind the step. Not yet!",
      bloodreaver: "On the hard nights the snake came back and dived straight across the room along a painted line! A broad one. We stood well to either side of it and let it go over. I'd have wrestled it, if the red allowed.",
      runeguard: "The omen, on the harder nights: the serpent returns and dives across the room along a painted line. The answer: stand well clear of the line, to either side, and let it pass. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "On the hard nights the serpent returned for a second helping, diving across the room along a painted line like a knife down a loaf. We stood well to either side of it and let the slice fall. Rich, and brief.",
      oathbroker: "On the harder terms the serpent returns and dives across the room along a painted line. The fine print: it is broad. The undersigned stand well to either side and let it pass. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "On hard nights the serpent returned and spoke once more, a dive across the room along a painted line, broad and loud. We stood well to either side and let it pass. Then we answered. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Hard nights: serpent returns, dives across the room along a painted line. Broad. Stood well to either side and let it pass. No cover to use. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "On the hard nights the serpent came back for an encore, diving across the room along a painted line, which is lazy. We stood well to either side of it and let it pass. It never saw me, but I saw it coming.",
      pyromancer: "On the hard nights the serpent came back, dazzling, and dived straight across the room along a painted line! I stood well to the side, applauded, and kept casting. Mostly unsinged, and mostly delighted.",
      thermist: "Cold read: hard nights, the serpent returns, dives across the room along a painted line. Broad. Stand well clear, either side. Hot read: my pulse went with it. Back to the middle, to one side of the line.",
      driftblade: "On the hard nights the serpent came back and dived across the room along a painted line, a broad one, and I ran well clear of it, along it, round it, and let it pass behind me, never landing, never in its road.",
      alembist: "Ailment: on hard nights the serpent returns and dives across the room along a painted line. Remedy: stand well clear, either side. Note: it is broad. Label: second coil, same cure.",
      threadweaver: "On the hard nights the serpent came back and dived across the room along a painted line, like a needle through cloth. A broad one. We stood well clear to either side and let it pass. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "On the hard nights the serpent made an encore: a dive across the stage along a painted line, broad as a trapdoor. The company stood well to either side and let it cross. (Exit, the serpent, stage right.)",
      cleric: "On the hard nights the serpent returned and dived across the room along a painted line, a broad one. I called my dears well clear to either side and let it pass. Thank the light for plain lines.",
      grovekeeper: "On the hard nights the serpent came back and dived across the room along a painted line like a flood through a field. A broad one. My lot stood well to either side and let it pass. Plant first, and stand on high ground.",
      chronomancer: "On the hard nights the serpent returns and dives across the room along a painted line a beat after it is drawn. A broad one. We stood well to either side before the beat. I'll have told them. I did.",
      tidecaller: "On the hard nights the serpent surged back through the room like a rip through shallows, along a painted channel. I kept to the slack water on either side of it, and so did we all, well away. It ran empty. Mind the tide.",
      lanternkeeper: "On the hard nights the serpent came back and dived across the room along a painted line. A broad one. I lit the ground to either side, well clear, and we all stood there while it passed. A light for each of us.",
      kenseier: "On the hard nights the serpent returned and dived across the room along a painted line. No beat I could meet; a broad line to read and keep out of. We stood well clear, either side, and it passed. Breathe, then strike.",
      houndmaster: "Hard nights, the big snake came back and dived across the room along a painted line. Broad. Whistled the dogs to one side, well clear, and let it by. Like a bull going through a gate. Heel.",
    } },
    'Chorus of the Fallen': { hard: false, learned: {
      bastion: "In his last dance all three struck in turn after the cuts, silver copies of Corvane, Brannoc and Morrow-Oak, and on the hard nights one joined every act. Corvane's cut ran through whoever stood farthest, so they stepped off. Brannoc's leap followed one, walked clear of the rest. Morrow-Oak's petals left gaps. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "In his last dance the dead came back, and on the hard nights one in every act: Corvane, Brannoc, Morrow-Oak, silver copies striking in turn after the cuts. Corvane's cut through the farthest of us, Brannoc's leap on one, the petals with their gaps. We had killed all three. I knew the sensation.",
      thresher: "In his last dance, dear, three old guests come as silver copies one after another after the cuts, and one in every act on hard nights. Corvane draws through whoever is farthest, so step off the line. Brannoc leaps after one of us, who leads him off. Morrow-Oak's petals have gaps.",
      bloodreaver: "The old ones came back in his last dance, one after another, and on hard nights one in every act. I knew each by its scar! Corvane's cut ran through whoever stood farthest, so we left its lane. Brannoc's leap chased one of us, who ran it clear. The oak's petals had gaps.",
      runeguard: "The omen, in his last dance and in every act on the harder nights: silver copies of three beaten foes, each with its known move, striking after the cuts. The answer: Corvane's cut falls through the one farthest from him; Brannoc's leap follows one of us, led away; Morrow-Oak's petals leave gaps. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "In his last dance my host reheated three old dishes as silver copies, once the cuts were served, and on the hard nights one in every act. Corvane's thin cut through the farthest guest; Brannoc's leap onto one plate, carried clear of the others; Morrow-Oak's petals, with gaps to sit in. Still hungry.",
      oathbroker: "In his last dance, and each act on the harder terms, three settled accounts are called back as silver copies, one after another after the cuts. Corvane's cut runs through the party farthest, who vacates the line. Brannoc's leap follows one party, who leads it from the rest. Morrow-Oak's petals leave gaps. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "Three old voices spoke again in his last dance, silver copies, one after another, and on hard nights one in every act. Corvane's long word fell on the farthest of us, who stepped aside. Brannoc's leap followed one of us, led clear. The oak's petals left quiet gaps, and I stood in one. Breathe.",
      ranger: "His last dance: old quarry as silver copies, all three, one after another once the cuts end. Hard nights: one in every act. Corvane's cut: through whoever's farthest off, so get out of the lane. Brannoc's leap: tracks one of us, take it wide. Morrow-Oak's petals: stand in a gap. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "In his last dance he borrowed three of my old marks as silver copies, one after another, and on hard nights one in every act, which is cheating. Corvane's cut through whoever stood farthest; Brannoc's leap on one, led wide; the oak's petals, with a gap to slip into. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "The old ones returned as silver copies in his last dance, one after another, and on hard nights one in every act. I could have wept! Corvane's cut through whoever was farthest, so step aside. Brannoc's leap came for one of us, who ran it clear. The petals have gaps. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Cold read: old foes as silver copies, all three after the cuts in his last dance, one in every act on hard nights. Corvane's cut through the farthest of us; step off. Brannoc's leap on one of us; lead it from the rest. The oak's petals; stand in a gap. Back to the middle.",
      driftblade: "The old ones came back in his last dance as silver copies, one after another, and one in every act on hard nights, and Corvane's cut ran through the farthest so I left its lane and Brannoc's leap chased one who ran it wide and the oak's petals left gaps, which I took, never landing.",
      alembist: "Ailment: old foes as silver copies, all three at the end of his last dance, and one in every act on hard nights. Remedy: Corvane's cut falls on the farthest of us, so leave the lane; Brannoc's leap follows one of us, who leads it away; Morrow-Oak's petals leave gaps. Label: old guests.",
      threadweaver: "In his last dance three old seams were stitched in one after another, silver copies each, and on hard nights one in every act. Corvane's cut ran through whoever stood farthest, so we left the lane. Brannoc's leap followed one stitch, who drew it clear. The oak's petals had gaps. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "In his last dance three old players took a curtain call as silver copies, one after another after the cuts, and on hard nights one in every act. Corvane's cut crossed the stage to the farthest, we cleared the lane. Brannoc's leap followed one player, who led it off. The oak's petals left gaps.",
      cleric: "In his last dance three poor souls returned as silver copies, one after another after the cuts, and on hard nights one in every act. Corvane's cut fell through whoever stood farthest, so my dears stepped aside. Brannoc's leap followed one of them, who led it clear. The petals left gaps. Dawn keep us.",
      grovekeeper: "The old ones came back in his last dance as silver copies, one after another, and one in every act on hard nights, like weeds in spring. Corvane's cut through the farthest; step aside. Brannoc's leap after one of mine, who ran it clear. The oak's petals had gaps to root in. Plant first.",
      chronomancer: "The old ones return as silver copies at his last dance's end, one after another, and one in every act on hard nights; I know each tune. Corvane's cut comes through the farthest of us a beat after its line; Brannoc's leap follows one, landing late; the petals leave gaps. I'll have known.",
      tidecaller: "In his last dance three old wrecks surfaced as silver copies, one after another after the cuts, and on hard nights one in every act. Corvane's cut ran through the farthest, so we drew clear. Brannoc's leap chased one of us, who led it clear. The petals left calm gaps. Mind the tide.",
      lanternkeeper: "In his last dance, and one in every act on hard nights, silver copies of three old foes struck one after another. I lit a spot clear of Corvane's cut, which falls on the farthest of us; walked beside the one Brannoc's leap followed, away from the rest; and lit a petal gap.",
      kenseier: "In his last dance three old teachers stood as silver copies, striking in turn after the cuts, and on hard nights one in every act. Corvane's stroke falls through the farthest, so we left the lane. Brannoc's leap follows one of us, who leads it clear. The oak's petals leave gaps. Catch the beat.",
      houndmaster: "His last dance, old game as silver copies, one after another after the cuts. Hard nights, one in every act. Corvane's cut through whoever's farthest, so out of the lane. Brannoc's leap after one of us, led wide of the dogs. Oak's petals with gaps to stand in. Dogs knew every one. Good dogs.",
    } },
    'Dark Ember': { hard: true, learned: {
      bastion: "On the hard nights a black ember rode one of us. It had to be carried to the very edge of the shadow and held there until it fell, and it pushed the shadow back. The rest kept off the edge. Anywhere else it burned the floor. Held.",
      gloomsworn: "On the hard nights a black ember rode one of us. It was carried to the very edge of the shadow and held there until it dropped, and the shadow drew back a step. Anywhere else it burned the floor. I know what a dark thing wants.",
      thresher: "On the hard nights a black ember rides one of us, dear. Carry it to the very edge of the shadow and hold it there till it falls, and the shadow steps back. Anywhere else it burns the floor. Do mind the step. Off we go.",
      bloodreaver: "On the hard nights a black ember rode one of my friends! Carry it to the very edge of the shadow, hold it there till it drops, and the shadow steps back. Anywhere else it burns the floor. I'd have carried it myself. A fine scar.",
      runeguard: "The omen, on the harder nights: a black ember upon one of us. The answer: carry it to the very edge of the shadow, hold it there until it falls, and the shadow is pushed back. Elsewhere it burns the floor. The rest stay clear. As foreseen.",
      gorgemaw: "On the hard nights a black ember rode one of the guests, like a burnt garnish. Carry it to the very edge of the shadow and hold it there till it drops, and the shadow shrinks. Anywhere else it burns the floor. Bitter, but useful.",
      oathbroker: "On the harder terms a black ember is levied upon one of the undersigned. The clause: it must be carried to the very edge of the shadow and held there until it falls, whereupon the shadow retreats. Elsewhere it burns the floor. So noted.",
      ironpalm: "On hard nights a black ember rode one of us, a quiet word. It was carried to the very edge of the shadow and held there until it fell, and the shadow drew back. Anywhere else it burned the floor. We answered with patience. Breathe.",
      ranger: "Hard nights: black ember on one of us. Carry it to the shadow's edge, hold it till it drops. Shadow steps back. Anywhere else it burns the floor. Rest stay clear. Clean line.",
      shadowblade: "On the hard nights a black ember rode one of us, which is a clumsy sort of dark. Carry it to the very edge of the shadow, hold it there till it drops, and the shadow retreats. Anywhere else it burns the floor. It never saw me.",
      pyromancer: "On the hard nights a black ember rode one of us, the one fire I was not allowed to love! Carry it to the very edge of the shadow and hold it till it drops, and the shadow retreats. Anywhere else it burns the floor. Mostly unsinged.",
      thermist: "Cold read: hard nights, a black ember on one of us. Carry it to the edge of the shadow, hold it there till it drops. Shadow steps back. Hot read: anywhere else, it burns the floor. Too far in, too late. Back to the middle, away from the edge.",
      driftblade: "On the hard nights a black ember rode one of us and had to be carried to the very edge of the shadow and held there until it dropped, so I ran it out along the rim, round, and stood, just once, and the shadow drew back and I never landed after.",
      alembist: "Ailment: on hard nights a black ember rides one of us. Remedy: carry it to the very edge of the shadow and hold it there until it falls; the shadow retreats. Note: anywhere else it burns the floor. Label: wrong place, wrong fire.",
      threadweaver: "On the hard nights a black ember rode one of my stitches. I watched them carry it to the very edge of the shadow and hold it there till it dropped, and the shadow drew back like a hem taken up. Anywhere else it burns. Mind the slack.",
      marionettist: "On the hard nights a black ember rode one of the company, a cue to cross the stage to the very edge of the shadow and stand there till it dropped. The shadow stepped back. Anywhere else it burned the boards. (Exit, the ember. Quietly.)",
      cleric: "On the hard nights a black ember rode one of my dears. They carried it to the very edge of the shadow and held it there until it dropped, and the shadow drew back. Anywhere else it burns the floor. I mended them as they walked. Dawn keep us.",
      grovekeeper: "On the hard nights a black ember rode one of my lot. Carry it to the very edge of the shadow and hold it there till it drops, and the shadow steps back, like frost from a fire. Anywhere else it burns the floor. Plant first.",
      chronomancer: "On the hard nights a black ember rides one of us, and drops a good while later. Carry it to the very edge of the shadow and hold it there till it falls, and the shadow steps back. Elsewhere it burns. I'll have walked it there. They did.",
      tidecaller: "On the hard nights a black ember rode one of us, like a stone sinking. Carry it to the very edge of the shadow, hold it there until it drops, and the shadow ebbs. Anywhere else it burns the floor. Wait for the water.",
      lanternkeeper: "On the hard nights a black ember rode one of us. I walked beside them with a light to the very edge of the shadow, where they held it till it dropped, and the shadow drew back. Anywhere else it burns the floor. I'll leave one burning.",
      kenseier: "On the hard nights a black ember rode one of us, with a count to its fall. Carry it to the very edge of the shadow, hold it there until it drops, and the shadow draws back. Elsewhere it burns the floor. Catch the beat.",
      houndmaster: "Hard nights, black ember rode one of us. Walked it out to the very edge of the shadow and stood there till it dropped. Shadow stepped back. Anywhere else it burns the floor. Dogs kept clear. Heel.",
    } },
  },
};
